# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# P81-123406 / BUG-24 — RemoteASN / ASN empty-struct rewrite
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The swagger declares RemoteASN and ASN as standalone schemas with no
# properties, so the codegen emitted `type RemoteASN struct {}` and
# `type ASN struct {}`. Both can never carry the integer ASN value they
# are supposed to represent — the API receives `leftASN: {}` instead of
# `leftASN: 65010` and rejects with:
#     leftASN must be a number
# We redefine each as a named int32 (`type RemoteASN int32`) so Go's
# default JSON encoding produces a plain integer on the wire. The
# Nullable* wrappers are kept for backwards compatibility.
#
# If a future swagger update gives these schemas a `type: integer`
# definition, drop these entries and let codegen regenerate normally.
model_remote_asn.go
model_asn.go

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# P81-124405 / BUG-26 — IPSecSharedSettingsCreate.p81ASN required→optional
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The swagger declares `p81ASN` as required on IPSecSharedSettingsCreate,
# but the public-api DTOs at
# perimeter81-public-api/src/api/entities/networks/tunnels
# /createIPSecRedundant.dto.ts mark it `@IsOptional()` on both
# v2.1 (IPSecRedundantSharedSettings) and v2.2
# (IPSecRedundantSharedSettingsV2_2). The codegen emitted a non-pointer
# `P81ASN RemoteASN` with no `omitempty`, so every CREATE serialized
# `"p81ASN": 0` on the wire, which the @IsValidASN validator rejects
# (range starts at 1). We switch the field to *RemoteASN with
# `omitempty`, mirror of the response type IPSecSharedSettings.P81ASN
# which is already *RemoteASN. Constructor signature and UnmarshalJSON
# requiredProperties list are updated to match.
#
# If a future swagger update marks p81ASN optional itself, drop this
# entry and let codegen regenerate normally.
model_ip_sec_shared_settings_create.go

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# P81-124405 — IPSecRedundantTunnel response strict-required
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Same family as BUG-25 sparse-meta fix. The swagger declares passphrase
# and remoteID as required on IPSecRedundantTunnel, but the public-api
# GET response omits passphrase (it's a secret — never returned on Read)
# and may omit remoteID when the user didn't set one explicitly. The
# codegen UnmarshalJSON strict-checked the full required list and failed
# every Read with `no value given for required property passphrase`,
# leaving terraform to discard the resource with `Root resource was
# present, but now absent`. We trim requiredProperties to the fields the
# upstream wire always emits: p81GWInternalIP, remoteGWInternalIP,
# remotePublicIP, remoteASN, gatewayID. Surfaced during BUG-26 live
# verification on tenant oleksandrc-test1.
#
# If a future swagger update marks passphrase/remoteID optional itself,
# drop this entry and let codegen regenerate normally.
model_ip_sec_redundant_tunnel.go

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# P81-124405 — NetworkTunnelIpsecRedundant strict-required trim
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The swagger declared 26 properties as required on
# NetworkTunnelIpsecRedundant (the list-network/GET-network response
# variant of a redundant tunnel in the NetworkTunnel anyOf union), but
# the wire response omits several:
#   - passphrase (secret — never echoed on GET)
#   - rightID, leftPrivateIP, rightPrivateIP, dpdAction (upstream-internal,
#     inconsistently returned)
#   - keyExchange/ikeLifeTime/lifetime/dpdDelay/dpdTimeout/phase1/phase2
#     (live only on the dedicated GET redundant tunnel endpoint, not on
#     the list-network response).
# Strict required check failed every Unmarshal → NetworkTunnel union
# fell back to NetworkTunnelBase → NetworkTunnelIpsecRedundant stayed
# nil → provider's getRedundantTunnelId couldn't extract the HA tunnel
# ID → Create returned without SetId → terraform reported "Root resource
# was present, but now absent".
# Trim to the always-present base fields plus haTunnelID (which is the
# whole point of this variant).
#
# If a future swagger update trims required itself, drop this entry.
model_network_tunnel_ipsec_redundant.go
